# Citation File Format v1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository" button on the repo page.
# Zenodo reads this file on release to mint a DOI and populate deposit metadata.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, schema, or methodology in academic or policy work,
  please cite it using the metadata below. Prefer the DOI once one is minted
  via the Zenodo integration (first tagged release).
title: "Cross-Layer Censorship Event Database"
abstract: >-
  A curated catalog of crypto censorship events (OFAC SDN, DOJ, SEC/CFTC,
  nation-state, corporate, supranational) tracked across six independent
  layers of the stack — network (L0), consensus (L1), RPC (L3), frontend (L4),
  asset on-chain, and off-ramp CEX — with precision-aware timelines and
  multi-source-verified evidence. Admission requires one primary source or
  two independent semi-primary sources per layer-level observation; every web
  citation carries a Wayback URL or local sha256 body_hash anchor for
  reproducibility. Released under an open schema so other researchers can
  extend the catalog.
type: dataset
